      "writtenOn": "2020-11-12T16:01:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After 3 attempts to generate MKBP interrupt this function is not changing state.interrupt to INTERRUPT_INACTIVE. As a result calling activate_mkbp_with_events() doesn\u0027t set MKBP interrupt and doesn\u0027t schedule force_mkbp_if_events() to be called by hook task. So we end up in INTERRUPT_ACTIVE, kernel is not able to respond (it is still rebooting) and we are neither able to repeat MKBP interrupt nor send next one.",
      "parentUuid": "f3135a6b_1ba41035",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 18
      },
