      "writtenOn": "2020-11-12T16:01:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, you are right. I just wanted to discuss if it is right direction for solving this problem.\n\nI was thinking a bit about this and it would be better to change force_mkbp_if_events() function to:\n\n\n static void force_mkbp_if_events(void)\n {\n         int toggled \u003d 0;\n \n         mutex_lock(\u0026state.lock);\n         if (state.interrupt \u003d\u003d INTERRUPT_ACTIVE) {\n                 state.interrupt \u003d INTERRUPT_INACTIVE;\n                 if (++state.failed_attempts \u003c 3)\n                         toggled \u003d 1;\n         }\n         mutex_unlock(\u0026state.lock);\n \n         if (toggled) {\n                 CPRINTS(\"MKBP not cleared within threshold, toggling.\");\n                 activate_mkbp_with_events(0);\n         }\n }\n\n\nMain difference is that this code doesn\u0027t ignore failed_attempts count and leaves INACTIVE interrupt state.\nLet me know what do you think about this.",
